## Attribution

VibeSpec is a simplified framework inspired by the following projects and ideas.
These projects are independent works by their respective authors and are NOT
included in this repository. VibeSpec contains only original code written
specifically for this framework.

### Origin

VibeSpec nace de un artículo: [Cómo unimos producto e ingeniería con agentes en Mercadona Tech](https://www.gemba.es/p/como-unimos-producto-e-ingenieria), escrito por [José Ramón Pérez Agüera](https://www.gemba.es) en [Gemba](https://www.gemba.es). VibeSpec es una versión simplificada de ese pipeline: misma disciplina, menos ceremonia. Sin José y sin Gemba, este framework no existiría.

*Spec first. Vibe right.*

### Ideas and Methodology

- **Working Backwards** (Bill Carr, Colin Bryar, Amazon, 2021) — The product-first
  thinking methodology that underpins the spec skill's approach to defining features
  before building them.

- **The Mom Test** (Rob Fitzpatrick, 2013) — The research methodology that influenced
  the emphasis on falsifiable, evidence-based Success Criteria.

### Source Projects

- **[Get Shit Done (GSD)](https://github.com/gsd-build/get-shit-done)** by Tâches —
  MIT License. VibeSpec borrows the concept of spec-driven development with
  falsifiable requirements, phase-based planning, and verification-before-completion.
  GSD's `.planning/` directory structure and REQ-ID traceability pattern inspired
  VibeSpec's SC-ID traceability. VibeSpec does NOT include any GSD code.

- **[Superpowers](https://github.com/obra/superpowers)** by Jesse Vincent —
  MIT License. VibeSpec borrows Superpowers' TDD-first philosophy (red-green-refactor
  cycle, no-production-code-without-failing-test rule, verification-before-completion
  principle) and the subagent-driven-development pattern. VibeSpec does NOT include
  any Superpowers code.

- **[Mercadona User Story Toolkit](https://github.com/josemerca/mercadona-user-story-toolkit)**
  by José Ramón Pérez Agüera — MIT License. VibeSpec borrows the "copiloto, no
  piloto automático" philosophy (the skill never invents data, forces the user to think),
  the anti-waterfall batch prioritization concept, and the spec-amendment pattern
  (never overwrite the original spec, record drift as amendments). VibeSpec does
  NOT include any Mercadona User Story Toolkit code.

### What VibeSpec Does NOT Include

- No code from GSD, Superpowers, or Mercadona User Story Toolkit is present in this
  repository. All skills, commands, agents, and hooks are original work written for
  VibeSpec.

- VibeSpec simplifies the 3-tool pipeline (GSD → MUST → Superpowers) into a single
  framework with 4 skills. The simplification is intentional: designed for solo vibe
  coders and small teams (1-3 people) who don't need PM/Eng role separation.

### What You Should Also Read

- [Cómo unimos producto e ingeniería con agentes en Mercadona Tech](https://www.gemba.es/p/como-unimos-producto-e-ingenieria)
  by José Ramón Pérez Agüera — The article that articulates the pipeline VibeSpec
  simplifies.